{"title":"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> have the property that the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88f211c45981e464bad66f719cb3fa6f802eaa30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   10 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   8 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   6 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   9 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   7 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"393\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have two different cases: one where there are two digits and another where there are three digits. There aren't many possible values for each case, so we can simply list them out.\n</p><p>If there are two digits, then the possible values are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values.\n</p><p>If there are three digits, then the possible values are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58d1eed7be2e1dcbfd4f7fe86fba2eb7566d8bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419924dabadec1cbc40ad235df6230a545e2161f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$102$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/1038785e77cdf7734f6ee2f8fed6de2ab19acc15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$201$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b4328d77715c539955c57ce1aee7b7bc9cdea458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values.\n</p><p>Altogether, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7d2338a3ea8117830fe1a8fd9e4fac335ed3e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 6 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"123\" height=\"30\" /> possible values.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we have two different cases: one where there are two digits and another where there are three digits.\n</p><p>If there are two digits, then we can have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> followed by a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values since there's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to do a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> but only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> way to have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> followed by a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If there are three digits, then we can have all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s, one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or we can have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> followed by two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s. The first and third have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible value each because there is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> way to have all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> followed by two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s. If there is one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the hundreds place cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities for the hundreds place. There are then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to order the other digits, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aae69d5a3cf3e7239ddd216b41562e0c55d903f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> possibilities. In total, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cca4f735a70c3fa2aca2d3a99c518ae456eb72b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 4 + 1 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> possible values for three digits.\n</p><p>Altogether, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7d2338a3ea8117830fe1a8fd9e4fac335ed3e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 6 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"123\" height=\"30\" /> possible values.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat\">2014 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 21 (page does not exist)\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 22 (page does not exist)\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 23 (page does not exist)\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"CEMC Fermat\">CEMC Fermat</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017132539\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 272/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2054/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 314/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8591/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.220      1 Template:CEMC_box\n100.00%    9.220      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3638